1
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,200
I came here to give you the money.

2
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,840
I had no idea Pong was going to show up.

3
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:13,840
‎PREVIOUSLY

4
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:16,240
If Grandpa won't give it to me,
then I won't ask.

5
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,760
I'll steal it.

6
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,000
-Grandpa.
-Father.

7
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,800
-Grandpa…
-Try to stay calm.

8
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,960
For you and Raiwin.

9
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,400
I'm not asking for much.

10
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:28,520
Just don't betray me or be ungrateful.

11
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,800
I'm tired.

12
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,880
Massage my feet.

13
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,720
Don't you think
you should repay me somehow?

14
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:04,560
Massage them.

15
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,120
Do you know

16
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:33,560
why I don't keep dogs or cats?

17
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,600
Because I'm afraid

18
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:46,160
that if I keep pets,

19
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,320
they might not obey me.

20
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,880
And if they won't obey me,

21
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:59,160
I definitely won't keep them around.

22
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,720
Keep massaging.

23
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:27,680
Mom, have Hathaya and Ramil
gone back to the house yet?

24
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:29,720
I haven't seen them.

25
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,840
They're probably still
at the hospital with Grandpa.

26
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:35,840
Hurry into Grandpa's room
and put everything back the way it was.

27
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:38,040
If they get home, they'll figure out

28
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,440
I was there to steal the money

29
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:41,680
and argued with Grandpa
before he fell down.

30
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:46,240
Ramil and Hathaya are back.

31
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,160
Hey.

32
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:51,720
Where are you going?

33
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,840
I'm going to Grandpa's room.

34
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,080
Grandpa is seriously ill.

35
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,760
You should be with him.

36
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,160
You claim you love him and then

37
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,800
come running home
because you want to be comfortable.

38
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,960
They don't allow visitors now.

39
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,280
I'll be going back soon.

40
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:10,880
Then why waste time going back and forth?

41
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,720
We have something to do.

42
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:16,680
What could possibly be
more important than Grandpa's life?

43
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,840
Finding out the truth.

44
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,560
We want to know
how he fell down the stairs.

45
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:25,080
We don't believe he left
his room by himself.

46
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:29,800
Let's go.

47
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:33,400
I said… I said don't go. Come back.

48
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,880
Hey, come back.

49
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,520
You can't go in there. Get out.

50
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,480
See? There's nothing here.

51
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,320
Wait.

52
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,840
What exactly are you two looking for?

53
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,800
You disobeyed me.

54
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:58,920
Get out. Get out of my house right now.

55
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,720
Go.

56
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,480
Pack your things

57
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,800
and get out of my house right now.

58
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:22,440
You don't have the right
to throw Ramil and me out.

59
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,400
That's right.

60
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,760
Mr. Pichai gave us permission
to live here.

61
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:31,000
Your Mr. Pichai is seriously ill.
He can't speak

62
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,400
or do anything.

63
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:35,320
As the daughter-in-law of this family,

64
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:39,480
it's my responsibility to manage
everything on Grandpa's behalf.

65
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:41,040
So I have full authority

66
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:43,520
to throw you two out. Go.

67
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:46,400
Don't be so heartless, Mom.

68
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,600
Hathaya loves Grandpa

69
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:56,800
and has helped take care of him.
Let her stay here.

70
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:59,640
Don't let her stay, sweetheart.
Throw her out.

71
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,280
Mom.

72
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:05,600
With Grandpa not staying here,
the house already feels lonely.

73
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:08,200
If we throw these two out too,

74
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:11,080
the place will feel even more depressing.

75
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:17,040
Well, you two can stay.

76
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,720
But stay in
that shabby little area of yours.

77
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,640
Don't show your faces around us again.

78
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,520
Go.

79
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,720
Chayanee.

80
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:33,880
What are you thinking?

81
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:36,000
Why keep a thorn in our side?

82
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:39,240
What if they turn around
and stab us in the back?

83
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,679
At first, I wanted them gone too.

84
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,720
But then I thought about it.

85
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,720
That wouldn't be satisfying.

86
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:52,600
I'm going to keep them close

87
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:54,960
and grind them into the dirt.

88
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,920
I'll send them back to where they started.

89
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:03,160
When they opened the door earlier,

90
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:05,600
my heart almost stopped.

91
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,400
Who did you send in
to clean up Grandpa's room?

92
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,280
I didn't send anyone.

93
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,880
I only called you.

94
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,080
Chamoi.

95
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:24,680
I knew those two would come
into Mr. Pichai's room.

96
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:28,000
So I hurried in and cleaned everything up.

97
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,560
What did you see before that?

98
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,400
I was cleaning the prayer room.

99
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,000
I heard shouting,

100
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:38,360
so I came out…

101
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,000
And what else did you see?

102
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,760
I saw you

103
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:46,040
push Mr. Pichai down the stairs.

104
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:54,520
Shut your mouth.

105
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,640
I didn't do that.

106
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,240
I saw it with my own eyes.

107
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,400
Mr. Pichai was trying to hold onto you,

108
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:02,160
and then you pushed him away.

109
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,720
Chamoi.

110
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:06,120
You know too much.

111
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,920
Chamoi.

112
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,080
Keep your mouth shut.

113
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,560
I'll give you 10,000.

114
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:13,400
This is serious.

115
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:15,560
I won't say anything.

116
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,640
But Madam, this is a huge deal.

117
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,240
Are you trying to blackmail me?

118
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:27,680
If I saw something this serious
and keep quiet,

119
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,440
that makes me guilty too.

120
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,600
I want one million.

121
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:36,600
That's too much.

122
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:41,000
It's not that much.

123
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:42,600
I saw you

124
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:45,520
take a lot of money from the safe.

125
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:46,840
Just one million,

126
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:49,920
and I promise I'll keep my mouth shut.

127
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:53,440
I'll be as silent as the dead.

128
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,080
Then die.

129
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:57,720
Come here.

130
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:59,080
Madam. Miss Chayanee.

131
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:02,080
-Don't, sweetheart. Let her go.
-Miss Chayanee.

132
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,960
Don't.

133
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:07,720
I'm not letting her go, Mom.
If I let her go, she'll talk.

134
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,480
And if she talks, I'll go to prison.

135
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:10,920
Chayanee.

136
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,880
Don't make this any worse
than it already is.

137
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,760
Let her go.

138
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,240
Miss Chayanee. I promise…

139
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:17,520
I won't say anything.

140
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,080
I don't want the money anymore.

141
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,680
-I don't want it.
-Don't hurt her.

142
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,440
-Let her go.
-Please.

143
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:25,600
Let me go.

144
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,720
Chamoi.

145
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,840
Listen to me.

146
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,880
I'll give you the money.

147
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:42,440
You have to stay here.
I'll take care of you.

148
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:46,040
No, madam.

149
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:49,720
I don't want anything anymore.
I don't want to die.

150
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,520
Please let me leave.

151
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,720
Chamoi.

152
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,680
You have to stay here.

153
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,360
You promised me.

154
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,400
Madam, please help me.

155
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:07,040
My mom is seriously ill.

156
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:10,720
We don't have enough money
to take her to the hospital.

157
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,000
Please help me.

158
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:15,840
I'll never forget this kindness.

159
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:18,800
I'll work myself to the bone for you.

160
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,800
Take your mom to the hospital right away.

161
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,720
I'll pay for her treatment.

162
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,600
Madam.

163
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:30,880
I… I've never forgotten

164
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:35,040
what you did for me.
I've always remembered your kindness.

165
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:36,400
That's why

166
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:40,640
I've been willing to work for you,

167
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:44,240
to be whatever you needed me to be.

168
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:47,520
Miss Chayanee.

169
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:52,680
I promise I won't say anything.

170
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:56,480
I'll keep my mouth shut.

171
00:12:56,560 --> 00:13:00,600
Please don't kill me.

172
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:02,880
Chayanee, sweetheart.

173
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,920
You need to calm down.

174
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:09,400
What happened to Grandpa
is already serious enough.

175
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:13,760
I don't want you creating another problem.

176
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,680
Here's what we'll do.

177
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,120
Only the three of us know about this.

178
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,640
It ends here. Alright?

179
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:26,000
Grandpa is still in the hospital.

180
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:28,240
What are you going to do next?

181
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,920
This is our opportunity.

182
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:33,840
We need to take control of everything.

183
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,760
Everyone already knows

184
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:48,680
that my grandfather is seriously ill
and will need a long period of treatment.

185
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:51,880
I'll be taking over management.

186
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:56,520
And here's management's first order.

187
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,360
Hathaya.

188
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,520
Pack your things
and get out of the office.

189
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:05,120
Grandpa put me in charge
of the project's accounts.

190
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,560
I can't follow that order.

191
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:12,160
Maybe I need to refresh everyone's memory.

192
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:15,000
The company president is currently ill.

193
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:17,880
As vice president,

194
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,120
I'm taking over management.

195
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:23,280
So management's orders

196
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:24,800
are final.

197
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,440
I'll handle all accounting
and finances myself.

198
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:30,160
And I'm ordering a full audit.

199
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:33,600
Your mother already stole money from us.

200
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,600
Maybe you embezzled some too.

201
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:39,760
If I find evidence,
you can get ready for prison.

202
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,160
Then what do you want me to help with?

203
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,760
Marketing?

204
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:49,000
You're talented.

205
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:52,560
Put you in marketing,
and you'd sell every single house.

206
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,320
That would be too easy.

207
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,600
Then what do you want me to do?

208
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:03,280
Go back to the construction site.

209
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:06,480
Back to where you started.

210
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,920
You do this to humiliate her.

211
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,120
You're moving her from accounting

212
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,360
just to send her

213
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:18,960
back to manual labor?

214
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,520
Ramil.

215
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,440
I'm showing my sister
a great deal of respect.

216
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:27,440
If I meant to humiliate her,

217
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,800
I'd send her to housekeeping

218
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:33,040
to scrub toilets.

219
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,520
Why am I sending her
to the construction site?

220
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:41,240
Because Hathaya
is so beloved by the workers.

221
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:45,760
She's their angel. Their beloved champion
of the low-class masses.

222
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:49,080
If she works construction herself,

223
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:53,200
I think our development
will be finished in no time.

224
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,800
I'll wrap up the accounting today.

225
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,200
I'll start at the site tomorrow.

226
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:05,440
No.

227
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:09,680
You're starting today. Right now.

228
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,360
Chamoi.

229
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,600
Yes, madam.

230
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:24,840
There's your low-level worker uniform.

231
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:34,920
Go on.

232
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:37,480
Get to work.

233
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:40,840
And don't disappoint your new president.

234
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:44,120
Go. Everyone, back to work.

235
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:07,560
They're awful.

236
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:09,680
They didn't fire you

237
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:13,960
only because they want
to pressure you and get revenge.

238
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:18,640
The more they see that Grandpa loves
and trusts me,

239
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:21,000
the more they want to grind me down.

240
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:24,640
Can you handle this?
You don't have to put up with it.

241
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:26,480
I'm not giving up.

242
00:17:27,319 --> 00:17:31,560
Grandpa is sick. I have to stay and
take care of his business as best I can.

243
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,360
I'm glad you're fighting.

244
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:39,760
Then…

245
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,960
I'll fight with you.

246
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:54,720
I'm going to work.

247
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:09,200
You see your older brother and you can't
be bothered to say hello or show respect?

248
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,120
I already told you.

249
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,680
When I look at you,

250
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,600
all I see is a mask

251
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,320
with your father's face on it.

252
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:24,720
You're not the Raiwin
I used to know anymore.

253
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:45,480
Congratulations to the new president.

254
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:49,080
Thank you.

255
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:58,760
When I came in just now, I saw
your sister wearing a worker's uniform.

256
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:03,480
I sent her somewhere she likes.

257
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:07,080
Why? Do you feel sorry for her?

258
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:09,160
Or do you want to go back
for someone low-class?

259
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:12,720
Hey.

260
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:16,640
I'm smart enough
to know who's good for me.

261
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:22,400
With a mouth that sweet,
what are you trying to get from me?

262
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,400
Can you help me with something?

263
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:28,320
I hate people who look down
on me and act like I don't matter.

264
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,080
Who do you mean?

265
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,440
Miss Hathaya. Don't carry that.

266
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:40,840
-It's fine. I can do it.
-No.

267
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,320
No. It's heavy.

268
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,240
Max, I've done this before.

269
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:47,000
My beautiful little Hathaya.

270
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:48,640
Go sit over there and look pretty.

271
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:51,040
-Exactly.
-Come on.

272
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,880
-You don't have to do this.
-Right.

273
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:54,560
We'll handle this part.

274
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:59,560
It's my job. The president ordered
me to do it, so I have to do it.

275
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:04,760
Boss. Come help.

276
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:07,400
I'm not letting Miss Hathaya
do heavy work like this.

277
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:11,040
Then why don't you supervise
the workers over there?

278
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:14,200
-But if--
-I'm the foreman.

279
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:15,920
You have to follow my orders.

280
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:20,960
If Chayanee finds out, she won't be happy.

281
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:24,480
Then when she comes,

282
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:26,920
we'll put on the show
she wants to see. Okay?

283
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,520
We'll stand guard and warn you.

284
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:34,360
-Okay.
-Go. Go rest.

285
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:37,560
Hey! The demon president is coming.
Everyone, back to work.

286
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:38,480
Go, go.

287
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:41,720
Hurry.

288
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:46,560
Well, Miss Chayanee, what's up?

289
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,240
What brings you to the site?

290
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,920
You almost never come here.

291
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:53,600
I don't want to be here.

292
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:56,760
It smells like sweat. And it smells like

293
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:59,120
mud and buffalo.

294
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,840
You've raised buffalo before,
Miss Chayanee?

295
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:05,200
Is that how you know
what mud and buffalo smell like?

296
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,240
Of course, I've smelled it.

297
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:10,000
I'm raising some right now.

298
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:11,360
A herd of cows and buffaloes.

299
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:13,840
-Hey.
-Hey.

300
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:14,960
Miss Chayanee.

301
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,840
When you say cows and buffaloes,

302
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:20,040
you don't mean us, do you?

303
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:22,280
Because none of us have horns.

304
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:24,920
And nobody

305
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,960
leads us around by the nose either.

306
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:32,200
What did you come here for?

307
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:35,440
We're working.

308
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:37,480
If you stay in the way,

309
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,520
things will slow down.

310
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,360
Stop working.

311
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:47,480
Which section should I work on then?

312
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:49,240
None of them.

313
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:51,520
You're fired.

314
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:55,200
You're firing me?

315
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:57,960
What did I do wrong?

316
00:21:58,560 --> 00:21:59,800
You didn't do anything wrong.

317
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:02,440
I can't stand your face.

318
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:05,680
I don't want to see you,
and I don't want to work with you.

319
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,040
Take the envelope and leave.

320
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,080
Chayanee.

321
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,560
If you're going to fire someone,

322
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:15,520
you need a reason.

323
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,360
You can't just act on your emotions.

324
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:20,080
Workers are protected by labor law.

325
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:22,800
If you do this, you could be sued.

326
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:23,920
Then sue me.

327
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,960
Go ahead. I have enough money to pay.

328
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:28,480
Ramil.

329
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:32,640
Let me give you some brotherly advice,
since we used to share a roof.

330
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:34,640
Just leave.

331
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:37,760
Your boss doesn't want you here. Why stay?

332
00:22:39,280 --> 00:22:42,920
I guarantee Chayanee
will pay you enough compensation.

333
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:45,560
I've worked to the best of my ability.

334
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:48,200
I'm not leaving.

335
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:52,120
Fine. If you won't leave, then don't.

336
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,400
I'm firing all of you.

337
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:57,280
Huh?

338
00:22:57,960 --> 00:22:59,080
Why are you doing this?

339
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:01,080
They've done nothing wrong.

340
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,080
Then leave.

341
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:07,200
And I'll keep the workers.

342
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:12,360
Go. Get out.

343
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,920
Those of you who used to wander
the streets can go back to wandering.

344
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,080
Go sell garbage.

345
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:19,000
And all the migrant workers

346
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:20,760
can return to your countries.

347
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:22,920
If any of you wants to sue me,

348
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,360
go ahead.

349
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:28,280
But I'm warning you.

350
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:31,360
Lawsuits don't end quickly.

351
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:34,080
They can drag on for a long time.

352
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:37,040
Where will you get money for a lawyer?

353
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:38,680
Let alone to get by.

354
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:44,920
Go. I fired you. Get out.

355
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,040
Pack your things and get out.

356
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:55,680
Go.

357
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:02,600
I'll leave.

358
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:08,120
You should've agreed from the beginning.

359
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:12,600
Look at the workers. They're so scared,
they're about to wet themselves.

360
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:26,000
Take the envelope and leave.

361
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:28,320
Don't linger where she has to see you.

362
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:42,600
-Boss.
-Boss.

363
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:56,080
Are you sure you want to quit?

364
00:24:58,320 --> 00:25:00,960
It's the only way to save the workers.

365
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:05,560
Chayanee is pressuring us
from every direction.

366
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:12,080
I can't even imagine what she'll do next.

367
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:15,680
But no matter what happens,

368
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:18,160
you have to stay here.

369
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:20,240
The workers need you.

370
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:23,920
I'll take care of them.

371
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:32,240
Don't just stand there.

372
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:36,880
Do I need to whip you
before you'll move and get back to work?

373
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:40,360
Still staring at me?

374
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:42,720
Keep moving, or I won't pay you anything.

375
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:46,320
Go back to the office.

376
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,640
Don't stay and get upset.

377
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:51,160
Good idea.

378
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:55,560
I'd rather sit somewhere with AC.
It reeks of mud and buffalo here.

379
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:02,160
I quit.

380
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:03,960
I quit too.

381
00:26:04,040 --> 00:26:05,200
I quit too.

382
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:07,160
-We quit too.
-We're quitting.

383
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:08,760
We all quit.

384
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:10,040
Think carefully.

385
00:26:10,760 --> 00:26:14,000
If you quit, what are you
going to do for a living?

386
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,480
We'll find new jobs.

387
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:20,360
We won't work for a power-hungry boss.

388
00:26:21,320 --> 00:26:22,560
We're human beings.

389
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,720
We're not buffaloes!

390
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,000
-Come on, everyone.
-Let's go.

391
00:26:28,080 --> 00:26:29,920
-Let's go.
-We're leaving.

392
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:34,120
Fine. Go.

393
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:37,280
Chayanee.

394
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:39,560
If you drive all the workers away,

395
00:26:40,080 --> 00:26:41,320
who's going to work for us?

396
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:43,120
I'll hire new ones.

397
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:44,800
I'm never begging them to come back.

398
00:26:44,880 --> 00:26:47,360
Good workers aren't easy to find.

399
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:50,680
They've been here a long time.
The project is almost finished.

400
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:53,880
Why not wait until the work
is done before firing them?

401
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:55,760
What do you expect me to do?

402
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:58,840
I am not lowering myself and begging them.

403
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:06,680
I'll handle this.

404
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:17,360
Quitting was the right thing to do.

405
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:18,640
Boss.

406
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:21,240
-Come on.
-Boss.

407
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:29,040
Wherever you're going, we're going too.

408
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:32,360
Going where? Why aren't you working?

409
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:34,920
-We quit.
-What?

410
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:37,520
We may be poor, but we still have dignity.

411
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:41,880
Exactly. We can handle hard work.

412
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:46,600
But I won't tolerate being abused

413
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:49,000
and oppressed like that.

414
00:27:49,840 --> 00:27:51,400
-Yes. We're not buffaloes.
-Yeah.

415
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:53,800
-Exactly.
-We're not buffaloes.

416
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:57,200
Hathaya, you don't need
to put up with it either.

417
00:27:58,560 --> 00:27:59,920
Let's work somewhere else.

418
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,400
Exactly.

419
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:03,760
All of us.

420
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:06,120
Ramil. Hathaya.

421
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:09,200
We're good at what we do. There are
plenty of places that would hire us.

422
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:13,000
I can't go.

423
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:15,560
I'm staying here.

424
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:20,520
Chayanee is deliberately oppressing you.

425
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:22,280
She sent you here from accounting.

426
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:23,840
She'll only treat you worse.

427
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,120
Hathaya.

428
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:29,280
Don't stay here serving
these heartless rich people.

429
00:28:29,360 --> 00:28:30,720
I have to stay.

430
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,440
I can't abandon this place.

431
00:28:39,760 --> 00:28:43,360
And I need to ask all of you
to stay and help me.

432
00:28:50,080 --> 00:28:52,600
You all know how much
Grandpa loves this development.

433
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:56,200
I promised him

434
00:28:56,280 --> 00:28:58,560
I would take the best possible care of it.

435
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:01,280
Now Grandpa is sick.

436
00:29:02,840 --> 00:29:04,840
We don't know when
he'll wake up or recover.

437
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:09,000
I'm going to keep this project going.

438
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:16,000
If you love Grandpa

439
00:29:16,840 --> 00:29:20,160
and you want him to wake up
and see his project completed…

440
00:29:23,920 --> 00:29:25,440
will you stay with me?

441
00:29:31,120 --> 00:29:32,320
Everyone.

442
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:34,840
Do it for Mr. Pichai.

443
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,640
The man who gave us a chance.

444
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:41,280
Everyone.

445
00:29:46,280 --> 00:29:47,760
Listen to me.

446
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:52,920
Chayanee didn't really mean
to insult or fire all of you.

447
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:54,520
So,

448
00:29:55,320 --> 00:29:57,280
I'll apologize on her behalf.

449
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:01,640
I want all of you to go back to work now.

450
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:03,120
Finish the project.

451
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:06,840
I'll make sure everyone can work happily

452
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:10,240
and there won't be
any more problems. Okay?

453
00:30:14,040 --> 00:30:15,520
Look at them.

454
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:18,600
They're so arrogant. Don't beg them.

455
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:20,400
Let's hire new workers.

456
00:30:28,640 --> 00:30:31,320
We're going back to work.
Why are you standing in our way?

457
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:38,960
But understand this. We're not going back

458
00:30:39,040 --> 00:30:41,680
because of you two. We're doing it

459
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:43,080
for Mr. Pichai,

460
00:30:43,160 --> 00:30:44,800
Ramil, and Hathaya.

461
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:52,080
Come on, everyone. Let's get back to work.

462
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:05,600
Let's go back to the office.

463
00:31:06,680 --> 00:31:10,040
You go ahead. I have something
to settle with my younger brother.

464
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:24,480
Aren't you wondering
why Chayanee fired you

465
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:26,040
when you do so much around here?

466
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,800
So this was your doing?

467
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:38,040
What do you want?

468
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:43,800
I'm just teaching you to know your place.

469
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,240
You grew up eating and living in my house.

470
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:49,640
You should know how to please me.

471
00:31:52,120 --> 00:31:54,480
Don't act like you're above me.

472
00:31:55,320 --> 00:31:57,000
You've really changed

473
00:31:58,240 --> 00:31:59,680
since becoming subdistrict chief.

474
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:04,400
You're just as power-hungry
as your father now.

475
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:07,880
Good. At least you understand
that I have power.

476
00:32:08,960 --> 00:32:11,840
But you don't have to kneel and beg.
I'm not that dramatic.

477
00:32:13,320 --> 00:32:15,480
Put your hands together
and pay your respects

478
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:17,120
and apologize for looking down on me.

479
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:20,960
Then I'll let you come back to work.

480
00:32:31,960 --> 00:32:32,880
The hand…

481
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:37,080
is important.

482
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,680
It can mean a lot of things.

483
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:42,760
If we put our palms together,

484
00:32:43,840 --> 00:32:45,840
it's like two decent people meeting

485
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:50,600
and showing mutual respect.

486
00:32:53,080 --> 00:32:55,080
But if we

487
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:56,840
close it like this,

488
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:02,160
it's something we can use
to defend ourselves

489
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:07,080
or fight an enemy.

490
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:17,800
You're the one who chose to make
a fist and declare yourself my enemy.

491
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:21,200
So get ready for what's coming.

492
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:24,120
Make sure your mom survives it too.

493
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,320
How are you, son?

494
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:53,200
Raiwin said you're living
with Hathaya now.

495
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:55,120
That's good.
You can take care of each other.

496
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:03,640
Mom.

497
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:05,160
Where's your wedding ring?

498
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:10,760
I was careless. I wore it while washing
dishes and it slipped down the drain.

499
00:34:11,719 --> 00:34:12,760
Did you lose it…

500
00:34:14,239 --> 00:34:15,560
or did someone make you sell it?

501
00:34:17,719 --> 00:34:18,960
I'm sorry.

502
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:23,280
I really wanted to save that ring
for you to use at your wedding.

503
00:34:25,679 --> 00:34:26,760
Forget the ring.

504
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:29,120
I don't want anything.

505
00:34:30,040 --> 00:34:31,320
I'm worried about you.

506
00:34:31,960 --> 00:34:34,600
You give him everything.
You surrender everything to him.

507
00:34:35,800 --> 00:34:39,199
When you're no longer useful and have
nothing left, he'll throw you away.

508
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:42,840
I won't wait to be thrown away.

509
00:34:44,080 --> 00:34:45,199
I'm leaving on my own.

510
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:49,800
I want to move out.
I want to live with you.

511
00:34:51,239 --> 00:34:52,679
Let's move somewhere together.

512
00:34:58,400 --> 00:34:59,480
I…

513
00:35:01,920 --> 00:35:03,360
I'm not ready yet, Mom.

514
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:12,240
I'm unemployed now. I was just fired.

515
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:18,240
We don't need a fancy new house.

516
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:22,120
We can rent a room.
I just want to live with my son. Please.

517
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:26,160
Mom.

518
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:29,560
Give me a little more time.

519
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:33,000
As soon as I find a job,

520
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:36,520
I'll come get you.

521
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:44,440
He must be back. I should go.

522
00:35:46,600 --> 00:35:47,960
I'll wait for you.

523
00:35:56,200 --> 00:35:57,240
What are you doing here?

524
00:35:57,840 --> 00:36:02,040
You were talking big. Didn't you say
you'd never set foot in this house again?

525
00:36:02,120 --> 00:36:04,720
So now you're eating your words? Pathetic.

526
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:06,880
I don't want to be here.

527
00:36:07,600 --> 00:36:09,680
But my mom happens to live here.

528
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:14,120
No job. No money. Nothing to eat.

529
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:16,680
So you came begging your mom for money?

530
00:36:16,760 --> 00:36:18,320
Let me tell you something.

531
00:36:19,760 --> 00:36:21,160
Your mom has nothing left.

532
00:36:21,840 --> 00:36:25,160
I sold every last thing she owned.

533
00:36:28,040 --> 00:36:31,840
And as for parasites like you,
who are living under my roof,

534
00:36:32,480 --> 00:36:35,400
let me make one thing clear,

535
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:38,520
everything your mom owns belongs to me.

536
00:36:38,600 --> 00:36:41,960
Even her life and every breath she takes.

537
00:36:50,080 --> 00:36:51,640
Remember this.

538
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,640
It won't be long

539
00:36:55,600 --> 00:36:57,680
before I take my mom out of here.

540
00:36:58,960 --> 00:37:03,280
I've been drilling it into her head
from morning until bedtime

541
00:37:03,360 --> 00:37:05,680
that she owes me everything.

542
00:37:06,680 --> 00:37:10,080
Your mom is very well trained.

543
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:15,160
But an ungrateful person
like you can't be trained.

544
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:18,880
Get out. Get out of my house. Get out.

545
00:37:40,760 --> 00:37:42,000
Where are you going?

546
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:46,720
Home. I finished my work.

547
00:37:46,800 --> 00:37:50,000
You can't leave yet.
You have to work overtime.

548
00:37:50,760 --> 00:37:53,040
There's your pay.

549
00:37:57,040 --> 00:38:00,680
I've been working all day, Chayanee.
I'm exhausted.

550
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:03,800
I can't keep going.
I'll finish it tomorrow.

551
00:38:05,800 --> 00:38:07,320
Fine.

552
00:38:08,560 --> 00:38:10,280
If you won't do it,

553
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:14,960
I'll call the workers back
and make them work until morning.

554
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:19,880
I'll do it.

555
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:24,200
If I come back tomorrow morning

556
00:38:24,280 --> 00:38:25,880
and you haven't finished,

557
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:28,920
I'll fire every worker.

558
00:38:40,800 --> 00:38:41,720
Chayanee.

559
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:45,560
If you make her work
day and night like this,

560
00:38:45,640 --> 00:38:47,840
she could die.

561
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:51,320
Good, Mom.

562
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:53,960
Then I won't have to kill her myself.

563
00:39:10,800 --> 00:39:12,200
Ramil.

564
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,160
Who are you calling?

565
00:39:21,160 --> 00:39:22,880
Hathaya isn't going to answer you.

566
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:26,440
Why do you have Hathaya's phone?

567
00:39:26,520 --> 00:39:28,880
Hathaya is working.

568
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:33,040
There's a strict rule here.
No phones while working.

569
00:39:33,640 --> 00:39:35,640
How many hours past
working hours is it now?

570
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:38,920
I ordered Hathaya
to work overtime all night.

571
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:41,720
You've been fired.

572
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:43,480
You have no right to enter the site.

573
00:39:44,560 --> 00:39:46,320
I'll call the police on you.

574
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:52,200
If I find out you snuck
into the development,

575
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:54,960
I'll fire every single worker.

576
00:40:21,880 --> 00:40:24,080
Hello, Max. Where are you?

577
00:40:25,360 --> 00:40:27,400
Chayanee ordered Hathaya to work overtime.

578
00:40:27,920 --> 00:40:29,200
Go help her.

579
00:40:41,160 --> 00:40:43,240
Let's go help Miss Hathaya.

580
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:46,360
That demon president
is vicious and heartless.

581
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:47,400
She can't be human.

582
00:40:47,480 --> 00:40:49,600
Some wandering spirit
must have possessed her.

583
00:40:50,240 --> 00:40:52,720
That's the only reason
she could be this hateful. Just wait.

584
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:56,360
If I ever get the chance,
I’ll slap the spirit right out of her.

585
00:40:56,440 --> 00:40:57,800
Come on. Hurry.

586
00:41:00,560 --> 00:41:02,120
Damn, that's bright. Who is it?

587
00:41:03,600 --> 00:41:04,680
Chamoi.

588
00:41:04,760 --> 00:41:06,840
That's right. It's me.

589
00:41:06,920 --> 00:41:08,800
-I'm going to help Miss Hathaya.
-No.

590
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:12,040
Your boss ordered Hathaya
to work all night.

591
00:41:12,120 --> 00:41:13,640
We'll help so she can finish faster.

592
00:41:13,720 --> 00:41:16,720
Miss Chayanee ordered
Hathaya to work alone.

593
00:41:17,320 --> 00:41:18,840
Stop sticking your noses into--

594
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:20,240
Hey!

595
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:22,160
Hey. This is going too far.

596
00:41:22,240 --> 00:41:25,000
We'll help for free.
We don't even want overtime pay.

597
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:26,520
Move, you wandering spirit.

598
00:41:26,600 --> 00:41:27,800
No. I'm not moving.

599
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:31,440
One call to Miss Chayanee

600
00:41:31,520 --> 00:41:36,480
and all of you get fired. Then your
precious Hathaya will really suffer.

601
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:41,320
Hey.

602
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:44,880
I said no. I'll really call.

603
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:50,760
Well? One little tap

604
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:52,440
and all of you are screwed.

605
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:57,840
Let's go back.

606
00:41:57,920 --> 00:41:59,360
Come on.

607
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:05,160
You people have no idea
who you're dealing with.

608
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:13,880
Come on.

609
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:15,760
Don't move so slowly.

610
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:18,360
I haven't slept either.
I want to go to bed too.

611
00:42:18,440 --> 00:42:20,120
But because you're working so slowly,

612
00:42:20,200 --> 00:42:22,000
I have to sit here and watch you.

613
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:26,440
If you want me to finish faster,

614
00:42:26,520 --> 00:42:28,160
come help me.

615
00:42:28,240 --> 00:42:30,360
No way.

616
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:32,960
Madam would kill me.

617
00:42:34,600 --> 00:42:36,440
Hurry up. Stop slacking.

618
00:42:51,680 --> 00:42:52,920
Grilled chicken.

619
00:42:57,120 --> 00:42:59,160
Who's grilling chicken around here?

620
00:43:22,240 --> 00:43:23,840
Who's grilling chicken out here?

621
00:43:25,560 --> 00:43:29,280
Look left. Look right.

622
00:43:32,960 --> 00:43:37,000
No owner? Then it's mine.

623
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:51,440
Hathaya.

624
00:43:51,520 --> 00:43:52,600
Hathaya.

625
00:43:52,680 --> 00:43:54,920
We came to help.
Then we'll finish quickly.

626
00:43:57,960 --> 00:44:01,360
Really, it's okay. I can do it.
You've all been working all day too.

627
00:44:02,200 --> 00:44:03,720
You're more exhausted than we are.

628
00:44:04,520 --> 00:44:05,960
Pitching in gets us done fast.

629
00:44:07,320 --> 00:44:09,000
Don't worry, Miss Hathaya.

630
00:44:09,080 --> 00:44:10,840
That crafty old Chamoi

631
00:44:10,920 --> 00:44:13,280
is probably dragging
the chicken into the water to eat.

632
00:44:18,800 --> 00:44:22,960
I'm not dragging any chicken
into the water. I'm not a monitor lizard.

633
00:44:23,720 --> 00:44:24,800
How the hell is she here?

634
00:44:25,800 --> 00:44:28,240
What? You think I'm stupid?

635
00:44:29,600 --> 00:44:33,360
Sorry. I saw through your little trick.

636
00:44:33,440 --> 00:44:36,440
I knew you'd find some way
to come help your boss.

637
00:44:37,280 --> 00:44:38,680
Go home.

638
00:44:38,760 --> 00:44:40,760
I'll grill you all the chicken you want.

639
00:44:40,840 --> 00:44:42,120
Just don't tell your boss.

640
00:44:42,720 --> 00:44:46,160
A hundred. A thousand.
I still wouldn't take them.

641
00:44:46,240 --> 00:44:48,560
Someone like me

642
00:44:48,640 --> 00:44:50,880
would never betray her employer.

643
00:44:50,960 --> 00:44:53,640
You're still not leaving?

644
00:44:53,720 --> 00:44:55,160
Fine.

645
00:44:55,240 --> 00:44:57,320
I'm calling her now.

646
00:44:58,120 --> 00:45:00,120
You want to challenge the system? Fine.

647
00:45:00,200 --> 00:45:02,080
Please go home.

648
00:45:02,160 --> 00:45:03,760
I really can handle this.

649
00:45:03,840 --> 00:45:06,400
I'm okay. Go.

650
00:45:06,480 --> 00:45:07,600
Well?

651
00:45:08,520 --> 00:45:09,880
-Fine.
-Auntie.

652
00:45:10,760 --> 00:45:13,280
What you said earlier about

653
00:45:13,360 --> 00:45:15,240
never betraying your employer.

654
00:45:15,320 --> 00:45:17,040
That's actually a really good principle.

655
00:45:17,120 --> 00:45:20,240
But with what you're doing right now,
let me tell you something.

656
00:45:20,320 --> 00:45:22,600
You should choose a good boss.

657
00:45:22,680 --> 00:45:24,600
Then maybe your life would get better too.

658
00:45:26,880 --> 00:45:29,040
Understand? Choose carefully.

659
00:45:29,560 --> 00:45:30,920
You might end up better off.

660
00:45:34,600 --> 00:45:36,000
That really hit me.

661
00:45:36,080 --> 00:45:38,960
Your boss calls us parasites, right?

662
00:45:39,040 --> 00:45:40,240
Yes.

663
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:43,120
Sure. Maybe we are parasites.

664
00:45:43,880 --> 00:45:46,880
But someone who works for bad people

665
00:45:47,680 --> 00:45:50,080
is just a low-class parasite.

666
00:45:52,160 --> 00:45:56,600
That one hurt. Right through the heart.

667
00:45:59,360 --> 00:46:00,400
Stop.

668
00:46:00,480 --> 00:46:01,960
That's enough.

669
00:46:02,040 --> 00:46:05,560
Enough. I can't even process
all this guilt fast enough.

670
00:46:05,640 --> 00:46:07,480
I'm not here to insult you.

671
00:46:07,560 --> 00:46:09,240
Then what do you want?

672
00:46:09,320 --> 00:46:11,760
-My chicken.
-Hey!

673
00:46:11,840 --> 00:46:15,160
My chicken.

674
00:46:15,720 --> 00:46:17,600
My grilled chicken.

675
00:46:17,680 --> 00:46:19,240
Chicken.

676
00:46:22,520 --> 00:46:24,840
Come on. Work faster.

677
00:46:24,920 --> 00:46:28,120
I have to sit here watching you.

678
00:46:29,680 --> 00:46:31,040
Hurry up.

679
00:46:34,040 --> 00:46:35,120
It's okay, Max.

680
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:37,600
You all did everything you could.

681
00:46:38,280 --> 00:46:39,880
Tell the workers to go get some rest.

682
00:46:40,760 --> 00:46:41,960
And thank everyone for me.

683
00:47:42,760 --> 00:47:44,000
Where is Chayanee going?

684
00:47:58,800 --> 00:47:59,800
What is she doing here?

685
00:48:01,720 --> 00:48:02,720
Did she

686
00:48:03,760 --> 00:48:05,000
come to see Hathaya?

687
00:48:28,400 --> 00:48:29,320
Chayanee.

688
00:48:37,760 --> 00:48:40,600
You've finished your work.
So there's nothing left for you to do.

689
00:48:42,320 --> 00:48:44,040
I'm done. I'm going home.

690
00:48:46,640 --> 00:48:47,880
You don't need to go home.

691
00:48:48,520 --> 00:48:50,040
I'll send you back myself.

692
00:48:50,680 --> 00:48:53,240
What are you doing? Let go of me.

693
00:48:53,320 --> 00:48:56,560
I'm going to do the same thing
I did to Grandpa.

694
00:48:58,400 --> 00:48:59,480
Miss Chayanee.

695
00:49:00,080 --> 00:49:00,960
Don't.

696
00:49:01,040 --> 00:49:03,480
No. No. Chayanee, don't.

697
00:49:03,560 --> 00:49:05,280
Let me go.

698
00:49:05,360 --> 00:49:07,040
Let go. Let go.

699
00:49:07,120 --> 00:49:08,960
No. Don't!

700
00:49:10,280 --> 00:49:11,080
Hathaya!

701
00:49:15,800 --> 00:49:16,920
Ramil.

702
00:49:20,120 --> 00:49:21,120
Ramil.

703
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:29,880
Hathaya.

704
00:50:06,480 --> 00:50:07,800
I'm sorry.

705
00:50:09,120 --> 00:50:10,840
It's okay.

706
00:50:19,920 --> 00:50:21,040
What do you want?

707
00:50:21,120 --> 00:50:23,440
-Get down on your knees.
-You don't have to kneel to anyone.

708
00:50:23,520 --> 00:50:25,240
Back off. It's none of your business.

709
00:50:25,320 --> 00:50:26,200
‎NEXT EPISODE

710
00:50:26,280 --> 00:50:28,600
Where are you going?
I told you to put it back.

711
00:50:28,680 --> 00:50:29,520
Stop it, Saksit.

712
00:50:29,600 --> 00:50:31,040
Why did you do this?

713
00:50:31,120 --> 00:50:33,400
-Your father has something--
-I told you already.

714
00:50:33,480 --> 00:50:34,640
I don't have a father.

715
00:50:34,720 --> 00:50:35,920
My father is dead.

716
00:50:36,840 --> 00:50:37,800
You parasite.

717
00:50:37,880 --> 00:50:40,320
You think you can stand over me like that?

718
00:52:34,640 --> 00:52:36,600
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
